# AISEO production runbook

## Services and environments

Deploy exactly two application services from the same image and shared `node dist/entrypoint.cjs` command. Set `SERVICE_KIND=web` on Web and `SERVICE_KIND=worker` on Worker. Staging and production must have separate Supabase projects, persistent Redis instances, TRON addresses and third-party credentials. Redis AOF is required; Postgres remains the job source of truth.

Web must receive only `DATABASE_APP_URL` as the migration-created `app_backend` role. Worker must receive only `DATABASE_WORKER_URL` as `app_worker`. They are deliberately created `NOLOGIN` until an operator sets passwords outside version control: `ALTER ROLE app_backend LOGIN PASSWORD '...'; ALTER ROLE app_worker LOGIN PASSWORD '...';`. Do not create extra roles or put passwords in migration files. Neither role may own tables or have BYPASSRLS. `DATABASE_ADMIN_URL` is limited to migration/admin jobs and is rejected by both runtime processes. A generic runtime `DATABASE_URL` is also rejected.

Use a direct connection when the service can reach Supabase over IPv6 (or the project has the IPv4 add-on); otherwise use Shared Supavisor Session mode on port 5432. Never use transaction mode on port 6543 with the current Prisma runtime because it does not support prepared statements. A Shared Supavisor username is `app_backend.<project_ref>` or `app_worker.<project_ref>`. Percent-encode passwords and include `sslmode=require`, an explicit `connection_limit` (default deployment target: 5 per replica), `pool_timeout=10`, and an `application_name`. Ensure `(Web replicas × Web limit) + (Worker replicas × Worker limit)` stays below the project's connection budget.

Web receives `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` and never `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`; global logout is performed with the verified user's JWT. Worker also never receives `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`. Deploy `supabase/functions/account-erasure` with JWT verification enabled and invoke it once per day from Supabase Cron using the platform-managed service-role authorization. Its only business-data permission is the audited `claim_due_account_erasures` RPC. Configure Turnstile secret, SMTP credentials, email verification, session lifetime and inactivity timeout inside the production Supabase project. Do not expose Turnstile/SMTP secrets to either application service.

The Web service exposes only `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` to the browser through a no-cache `/runtime-config.js` allowlist. Do not configure production Supabase values as Docker build arguments; changing either runtime value only requires a Web restart.

Run SQL migration before application deployment. A migration failure blocks deployment. `/api/health/live` checks only the process. `/api/health/ready` requires Postgres, Redis, current migration and a recent Worker heartbeat. Optional provider status is separate.

## Release verification

Required CI gates: lockfile install, Prisma validation/generation, TypeScript, unit coverage, Supabase reset, SQL lint, pgTAP RLS/grants, Prisma drift, production build, container syntax startup, high-severity dependency audit and secret scan.

Staging must complete real GSC authorization/sync, a real DataForSEO scan, WordPress credential verification, publication and rollback, a low-value mainnet TRC20 transfer, ledger zero-difference reconciliation, and a Supabase PITR restore rehearsal. Mark all staging funds and records as test operations.

Do not open public registration or充值 until CI is green, Critical/High findings are zero, queues have run 24 hours without stuck work, alert drills pass, RPO 15 minutes/RTO 2 hours are demonstrated, and counsel signs the service, privacy, AI/content, acceptable-use and USDT/refund terms.

## Monitoring and incident response

Configure `SENTRY_DSN` and `VITE_SENTRY_DSN`. Alerts cover unhandled API/Worker failures, payment verification, ledger mismatch, queue backlog, dead-letter jobs and Worker readiness. Provider errors include trace/job IDs but never credentials. Configure infrastructure alerts for Supabase backups/PITR, Redis persistence and service restarts.

For a ledger mismatch, stop paid job creation and payment crediting, preserve logs and database snapshots, and reconcile from append-only ledger entries before resuming. Never edit or delete ledger rows. Corrections use an audited `ADJUSTMENT` entry.

For Redis loss, restore Redis if available and keep the Worker running; reconciliation deterministically recreates queued jobs from `job_runs`. Never manufacture successful job states.

## Backup and deletion

Use a paid Supabase production plan with PITR and backups. Target RPO is 15 minutes and RTO is 2 hours. Perform restore drills before launch and quarterly. Account deletion revokes Supabase sessions, disables solely-owned organizations immediately, and erases content/credentials after 30 days. Financial and audit records are retained in de-identified form according to counsel-approved retention periods.
